Description: NetworkManager front-end with tray applet and connection editor [Trinity]
 tde-nmctl manages network connections in the Trinity Desktop Environment
 through NetworkManager. It is modelled on network-manager-gnome (nm-applet
 and nm-connection-editor), nm-tray and plasma-nm.
 .
 The tray applet shows the network state and signal strength, lists the
 Wi-Fi networks in range, connects and disconnects with one click, asks for
 Wi-Fi and VPN passwords, switches networking, Wi-Fi and mobile broadband on
 and off, and shows notifications and connection details.
 .
 The connection editor handles wired, Wi-Fi (WEP, WPA/WPA2/WPA3 Personal and
 Enterprise, hotspot), 802.1X, VPN (OpenVPN, vpnc, OpenConnect, L2TP, PPTP,
 strongSwan and other plugins, import and export), WireGuard, mobile
 broadband, DSL/PPPoE, InfiniBand, bond, bridge, team, VLAN and dummy
 connections with their IPv4, IPv6 and proxy settings. It is available as
 an application, as a Trinity Control Center module (Internet & Network)
 and in System Settings.
 .
 Passwords that belong to the user are kept in TDE Wallet; changes that need
 administrator rights are authorized by polkit through polkit-agent-tde.
